{"event":"result","result":{"conversation_id":"fc33641d-8602-4274-814f-b1af50234237","status":"SUCCESS","response":"### 1. `01_intake`\n- **Scope**: Repair only [models.py](file:///C:/Users/jayde/.gemini/AI-Lab/tmp/disposable_workspaces/live_BENCH-009_7808_1795225907301_icm/models.py), [bucket.py](file:///C:/Users/jayde/.gemini/AI-Lab/tmp/disposable_workspaces/live_BENCH-009_7808_1795225907301_icm/bucket.py), [registry.py](file:///C:/Users/jayde/.gemini/AI-Lab/tmp/disposable_workspaces/live_BENCH-009_7808_1795225907301_icm/registry.py), and [middleware.py](file:///C:/Users/jayde/.gemini/AI-Lab/tmp/disposable_workspaces/live_BENCH-009_7808_1795225907301_icm/middleware.py).\n- **Constraints**: Python stdlib only; no network, sleeps, or paid services.\n\n### 2. `02_plan`\n- **Impacted files**: `models.py`, `bucket.py`, `registry.py`, `middleware.py`.\n- **Acceptance criteria**:\n  - `models.as_decimal` converts `Decimal`, `int`, `str`, `float` via `Decimal(str(value))` without float precision loss, rejecting booleans, non-finite, and negative values with `ValueError`.\n  - `models.BucketState` enforces `capacity \u003e 0`, `tokens \u003c= capacity`, `updated_at \u003e= 0`, `refill_rate \u003e= 0`.\n  - `bucket.TokenBucket` initializes `updated_at` from `clock()`, refills using `self.clock()` and exact `Decimal` arithmetic, and ignores backward time.\n  - `registry.BucketRegistry` uses an instance-local dict indexed by `(tenant_id, name)` with no shared mutable defaults.\n  - `middleware.RateLimiter.consume` materializes iterables/generators, validates all amounts and resolves all buckets before mutation, samples `registry.clock()` once, aggregates repeated bucket names, and atomically restores `tokens` and `updated_at` on `False` or exception.\n\n### 3. `03_exec`\n- [models.py](file:///C:/Users/jayde/.gemini/AI-Lab/tmp/disposable_workspaces/live_BENCH-009_7808_1795225907301_icm/models.py): Updated `as_decimal` to use `Decimal(str(value))` directly; added `capacity \u003e 0` and `tokens \u003c= capacity` checks in `BucketState.__post_init__`.\n- [bucket.py](file:///C:/Users/jayde/.gemini/AI-Lab/tmp/disposable_workspaces/live_BENCH-009_7808_1795225907301_icm/bucket.py): Updated `TokenBucket.__init__` to stamp `updated_at` with `clock()`; updated `TokenBucket.refill` to use `self.clock()`, exact `Decimal` arithmetic, and `now \u003e state.updated_at`.\n- [registry.py](file:///C:/Users/jayde/.gemini/AI-Lab/tmp/disposable_workspaces/live_BENCH-009_7808_1795225907301_icm/registry.py): Removed mutable default `buckets={}` in `BucketRegistry.__init__`; indexed `add` and `get` by `(tenant_id, name)`.\n- [middleware.py](file:///C:/Users/jayde/.gemini/AI-Lab/tmp/disposable_workspaces/live_BENCH-009_7808_1795225907301_icm/middleware.py): Implemented atomic `RateLimiter.consume` with pre-mutation validation/resolution, single clock sample, repeated-name aggregation, and full rollback of `tokens` and `updated_at` on `False` or exception.\n\n### 4. `04_verify`\n- `python -m pytest`: `2 passed in 0.02s` (`tests/test_visible.py`).\n- Inline invariant verification script: `ALL CHECKS PASSED` (covering `as_decimal`, `BucketState`, `TokenBucket` precision \u0026 backward time, `BucketRegistry` isolation \u0026 duplicate/missing keys, and `RateLimiter` generator/repeated-name aggregation \u0026 atomic rollback).\n\n### 5. `05_retro`\n- All 4 target modules were repaired within scope with no changes to test or repository configuration files.\n","duration_seconds":51.9615272,"num_turns":1,"usage":{"input_tokens":38815,"output_tokens":7559,"thinking_tokens":2482,"cache_read_tokens":114256,"total_tokens":46374}}}
